# 18. Implement Render Scheduler

### Task

Convert many input events into a controlled number of rendering passes.

### Required state

```text
render_pending = false
dirty_flags
```

### On invalidation

If:

```text
render_pending == true
```

do nothing except preserve the dirty flags.

If:

```text
render_pending == false
```

schedule one render.

### Conceptual sequence

```text
mouse event 1
    ↓
invalidate
    ↓
schedule render

mouse event 2
    ↓
invalidate
    ↓
render already pending
    ↓
do not schedule another

mouse event 3
    ↓
invalidate
    ↓
render already pending
    ↓
do not schedule another

scheduled callback
    ↓
one render
```

Therefore:

```text
20 events
→ potentially 1 render
```

rather than:

```text
20 events
→ 20 renders
```

---

# 19. Implement Rendering Order

The final rendering pipeline must remain:

```text
DATA
  ↓
VIEWPORT
  ↓
SCALE
  ↓
GEOMETRY
  ↓
STYLE
  ↓
RENDERER
  ↓
CANVAS
```

### Full candle pipeline

```text
OHLCV
 ↓
logical index
 ↓
visible range
 ↓
logical index → x
 ↓
price → y
 ↓
candle width
 ↓
body/wick geometry
 ↓
bull/bear state
 ↓
color
 ↓
Canvas line/rectangle
```

### Do not reverse dependencies.

For example:

```text
Canvas
  ↓
Data
```

is prohibited.

The renderer must not retrieve unrelated chart state.

---

# 20. Implement Density Mode

### Normal mode

Condition:

```text
bar_spacing >= 1.0 px
```

Action:

```text
render normal candles
```

### Dense mode

Condition:

```text
bar_spacing < 1.0 px
```

Action:

```text
enable density-aware processing
```

### Conflation candidate

Condition:

```text
screen-space separation < 0.5 px
```

Action:

```text
consider aggregation
```

### Aggregation

For N source candles:

```text
open  = first.open
high  = maximum high
low   = minimum low
close = last.close
volume = sum(volume)
```

This preserves OHLC semantics.

---

# 21. Implement Right Offset

### Initial value

```text
right_offset = 5 bars
```

Recommended adjustable range:

```text
5–10 bars
```

### Example

If:

```text
last_index = 999
right_offset = 5
```

the latest candle is positioned relative to:

```text
logical position ≈ 1004
```

leaving approximately:

```text
5 bars
```

of future space.

### User-scrolled state

If the user manually pans away from the latest candle:

```text
do not automatically force viewport back
```

unless an explicit "follow latest" mode is enabled.

---

# 22. Implement New-Data Update

### New candle

```text
append candle
    ↓
increment data count
    ↓
invalidate data
    ↓
update visible range if following latest
    ↓
update price scale if required
    ↓
schedule render
```

### Existing live candle

If timestamp/logical index already exists:

```text
update OHLCV
    ↓
recalculate affected geometry
    ↓
update price range if high/low changed
    ↓
schedule render
```

### Important

Do not rebuild all historical candles because the latest candle changed.

---

# 23. Implement Resize

### Inputs

```text
new_canvas_width
new_canvas_height
```

### Steps

```text
update dimensions
    ↓
visible_bars = width / bar_spacing
    ↓
update visible_to
    ↓
recalculate price-scale data_height
    ↓
recalculate visible candle geometry
    ↓
recalculate grid
    ↓
update crosshair if necessary
    ↓
schedule render
```

