# 24. Performance Rules

## Calculate once

Calculate once until configuration changes:

```text
colors
minimum spacing
zoom divisor
wick width
overscan
grid style
crosshair style
```

## Calculate when data changes

```text
data count
data index
price-range statistics
aggregation cache
```

## Calculate when viewport changes

```text
visible_from
visible_to
render_first
render_last
visible_bars
```

## Calculate when zoom changes

```text
bar_spacing
candle_width
x coordinates
visible range
```

## Calculate when price range changes

```text
price-to-y transformation
high_y
low_y
open_y
close_y
```

## Calculate for every visible candle

Only:

```text
OHLC retrieval
center_x
open_y
high_y
low_y
close_y
body geometry
wick geometry
bull/bear state
Canvas update
```

## Calculate for every mouse event

Only:

```text
mouse coordinate
logical coordinate
crosshair coordinate
pan delta
zoom anchor
```

depending on event type.

---

# 25. Operations Prohibited From Hot Loops

Do not perform these inside the per-candle loop:

```text
atan()
```

unless candle width actually depends on a spacing change.

Do not perform:

```text
color configuration lookup
```

through expensive object traversal.

Do not perform:

```text
full data scan
```

Do not perform:

```text
visible-range calculation
```

Do not perform:

```text
price-range discovery over entire dataset
```

Do not perform:

```text
Canvas item creation
```

if a reusable item exists.

Do not perform:

```text
Canvas item deletion
```

during ordinary panning.

Do not perform:

```text
indicator recalculation
```

for every candle during viewport movement.

---

# 26. Boundary Conditions

## Empty dataset

```text
data_count = 0
```

Render:

```text
background
grid if appropriate
crosshair if appropriate
```

Do not attempt candle access.

## One candle

```text
visible range may contain fractional positions
```

Clamp render index to:

```text
0
```

## Zoom minimum

```text
bar_spacing = 0.5
```

Further zoom-out must not reduce spacing.

## Very large spacing

Example:

```text
bar_spacing = 100
```

Candle width remains constrained by the width formula and does not exceed:

```text
bar_spacing
```

## Zero price range

If:

```text
high == low
```

avoid division by zero.

## Fractional viewport

Valid:

```text
visible_from = -4.73
visible_to = 195.42
```

Do not round these values.

## Negative logical positions

Allowed because the right/left viewport may contain empty space before the first data point.

## Pan beyond dataset

Clamp according to configured chart behavior, but do not destroy fractional positioning.

