# CORE ARCHITECTURAL CONTRACT

Every implementation task must preserve this dependency direction:

```text
DATA
  ↓
VIEWPORT / STATE
  ↓
SCALE
  ↓
GEOMETRY
  ↓
STYLE
  ↓
RENDERER
  ↓
CANVAS
```

The most important runtime contract is:

```text
USER EVENT
    ↓
UPDATE MINIMUM STATE
    ↓
INVALIDATE
    ↓
COALESCE
    ↓
RENDER SCHEDULE
    ↓
VISIBLE RANGE
    ↓
SCALE
    ↓
GEOMETRY
    ↓
STYLE
    ↓
REUSE CANVAS ITEMS
    ↓
CANVAS
```

The implementation must **never** turn:

```text
mouse movement
```

into:

```text
full dataset calculation
+
full geometry rebuild
+
Canvas deletion
+
Canvas recreation
```

The target architecture instead turns it into:

```text
mouse movement
→ small state change
→ dirty flag
→ one scheduled render
→ visible range
→ cached transformations
→ reused Canvas objects
```

That is the core mechanism responsible for achieving the TradingView/Lightweight-Charts-like interaction model in a Tkinter Canvas implementation.
